## Third-party dependencies

No third-party source code is vendored in this repository. Every dependency is
fetched by Cargo at build time, at the version its lockfile names.

Every release archive — the system's (`cargo xtask release`), the relay's and
the vault's (`cargo xtask release-server relay|vault`) — carries a file named
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES at its top. It is generated by the release verb from the
lockfiles the archive was built from, and never written by hand:

- which packages: exactly the ones the archive's build compiles, as
  `cargo tree` resolves that build — its binaries, features and target —
  over normal and build dependencies, never a dev-dependency;
- for each: its name, version, SPDX license expression and source, and the
  license, copying and notice files the package carries, each distinct text
  written out once; for a crate that compiles C sources under their own
  license (SQLCipher in libsqlite3-sys, OpenSSL in openssl-src), that
  license too;
- the head of the file names each lockfile, its sha256 and the target it was
  resolved for.

The code is `xtask/src/license_check.rs`. To read one without building an
archive:

    cargo xtask third-party-notices system|relay|vault

`cargo xtask license-check`, part of `just lint`, holds every dependency of
every shipped workspace to a list of permissive licenses and MPL-2.0, and a
release verb refuses to write a notices file naming anything else. MPL-2.0
applies only to the MPL-2.0 files themselves; Kotton's own source is not
subject to it, and each such package's source is at the address its row names.
